  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2f97d5a259ae472d8180193516c16ff7, type: 3}
  m_Name: redgate-risk-compliance-presales
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::JobListingData
  jobId: redgate-risk-compliance-presales
  companyName: Redgate Financial Risk
  roleTitle: Risk & Compliance Presales Consultant
  jobCardSummary: Compliance-heavy presales role with less deep technical demand,
    more process and stakeholder pressure.
  difficultyProfile: Commercial / compliance bureaucracy
  recruiterName: Eleanor Shaw
  recruiterTitle: Risk Solutions Recruiting Lead
  recruiterCompany: Redgate Financial Risk
  summary: Redgate Financial Risk is hiring a presales consultant to support regulated
    financial customers through risk, compliance, procurement, and legal review.
    The technical bar is less architecture-heavy than Helios, but the process language
    suggests careful stakeholder management and slow-moving committees.
  responsibilities:
  - Support discovery with risk, compliance, procurement, and security stakeholders.
  - Translate product capability into careful regulatory and business-value language.
  - Prepare customer-facing material for committees that need defensible claims.
  - Coordinate with sales and legal teams when customer expectations become ambiguous.
  requirements:
  - Experience with compliance, risk, governance, or regulated customer environments.
  - Commercial judgement when technical claims may have legal or audit implications.
  - Patience with multi-stakeholder evaluation and formal buying processes.
  - Ability to communicate clearly without overstating control coverage.
  niceToHaves:
  - Financial services customer experience.
  - Familiarity with audit evidence, policy mapping, or third-party risk workflows.
  - Comfort presenting to mixed legal, risk, security, and executive audiences.
  salaryRange: Stable compensation range with bonus potential described as tied to
    regional performance.
  processNotes: Recruiter screen, stakeholder-fit discussion, final customer-scenario
    round. The process may move slowly because legal and risk teams are involved.
  redFlags:
  - Bureaucracy and legal review may slow decisions after strong conversations.
  - The listing uses careful language around customer commitments and control claims.
  - Success may depend on navigating committees more than solving technical problems.
  greenFlags:
  - The role rewards precise communication and commercial patience.
  - Deep cloud architecture is less central than credibility with regulated stakeholders.
  - The company appears to understand compliance buyer complexity.
  defaultRoleFitDelta: 1
  defaultRecruiterTrustDelta: 0
  defaultCandidateConfidenceDelta: 0
  defaultEnergyDelta: -1
  defaultOverclaimRiskDelta: 0
  defaultTechnicalReadinessDelta: -1
  defaultRapportMomentumDelta: 1
  defaultRoomProfileId: InterviewRoom-ComplianceCommercial
  roomContextLine: Redgate shifts the pressure toward careful claims, stakeholder
    patience, and compliance ambiguity.
  outcomeContextLine: The panel weighed commercial care, compliance judgement, and
    patience with process drag.
  processSummaryNote: Redgate was the commercial/compliance opportunity with heavier
    process pressure.
